#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#            ESA Debris Risk Assessment and Mitigation Analysis Tool            
#            MASTER-based Impact Flux and Damage Assessment Software
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#                               DRAMA - MIDAS
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Note:  "midas.ble" specifies parameters for the user defined ballistic limit 
#        equations. In the first block the parameters for single wall equations 
#        are defined. Parameters defined in the second block are for the use of
#        the multiple wall equation.
#        Only user defined parameters are listed below. Four BLE's are coded in
#        the MIDAS software (two single wall and two multiple wall equations)
#
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#===============================================================================
#
#------------------< Single Wall Ballistic Limit Equation >---------------------
# Note: The single wall BLE as shown below is implemented in the software MIDAS
#       together with two hard coded parameter sets. If the defined type 
#       of BLE is "3" the damage assessment of MIDAS will use the below defined 
#       parameters.
#       ==> max. 10 parameter sets can be defined
#       ==> if no single wall BLE is defined at least one line has to be blank
#
#       Column 1   : Number of BLE in ascending order
#       Column 2-8 : BLE parameters 
#       Column 8   : Name of the BLE (char*30)
#
# EXAMPLE:
# 1    1.10 0.5665  1.056  0.500  0.66667  0.66661  -1.500  Example 01
#
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No.  Kf   K1      lambda beta   gamma    xi       kappa   Description
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  1.80  0.6200  1.000  0.500  0.66667  0.66667 -0.500 CFRP Single Wall
   2  1.20  0.5665  1.056  0.500  0.66667  0.66662 -2.500 SW Example 2
   3  1.30  0.5665  1.056  0.500  0.66667  0.66663 -3.500 SW Example 3
   4  1.40  0.5665  1.056  0.500  0.66667  0.66664 -4.500 SW Example 4
   5  1.50  0.5665  1.056  0.500  0.66667  0.66665 -5.500 SW Example 5
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#===============================================================================
#
#-----------------< Multiple Wall Ballistic Limit Equation >--------------------
# Note: The multiple wall BLE as shown below is implemented in the software MIDAS
#       together with two hard coded parameter sets. If the above defined type 
#       of BLE is "6" the damage assessment of MIDAS will use the below defined 
#       parameters.
#       ==> max. 10 parameter sets can be defined
#       ==> if no single wall BLE is defined at least one line has to be blank
#
#       Column 1    : Ascending numbering of BLE and identifiere in first ; 
#                     "-" in second and third line of parameter set
#       Column 2    : Velocity boundary for the given parameters
#       Column 3-13 : BLE parameters
#
# 1  Example 1
# -  3.0  0.5535  0.9225  1.056  0.5  0.66667  0.0  0.0  1.6667  0.0  0.0  1.0
# -  6.0  0.5535  0.9225  1.056  0.5  0.66667  0.0  0.0  1.6667  0.0  0.0  1.0
#
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No. vel  K1      K2      lambda beta gamma    kappa delta zeta   nu1  nu2  mue
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  MW Example 1
  -   3.0   0.5535   0.9225   1.056   0.5   0.66667   0.0   0.0   1.6667   0.0   0.0   1.0
  -   6.0   0.5535   0.9225   1.056   0.5   0.66667   0.0   0.0   1.6667   0.0   0.0   1.0
   2  MW Example 2
  -   3.0   0.5535   0.9225   1.056   0.5   0.66667   0.0   0.0   1.6667   0.0   0.0   1.0
  -   6.0   0.5535   0.9225   1.056   0.5   0.66667   0.0   0.0   1.6667   0.0   0.0   1.0
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#================================================================================
#
#--------------< Schaefer-Ryan-Lambert Ballistic Limit Equation >----------------
# Note: The Schaefer-Ryan-Lambert BLE as shown below is implemented in the software
#       MIDAS together with two hasrd coded parameter sets. If the above defined type
#       of BLE is '9' the damage assessment of MIDAS will use the below defined
#       parameters.
#       ==> max. 10 parameter sets can be defined
#       ==> if no Schaefer-Ryan-Lambert BLE is defined at least one line has to be blank
#
#       Column 1    : Ascending numbering of BLE and identifiere in first ;
#                     '-' in second line of parameter set
#       Column 2-3  : Velocity boundaries for the ballistic/shatter/hypervelocity regimes
#       Column 4-15 : BLE parameters
#
# 1  Example 1
# -  3.0  7.0  3.0  1.4  0.1  0.4  1.5  0.5  0.6667  0.3333  1.3333  1.25  2.6667  2.5
#
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No. v1   v2   Kmli K3s  K2s  K3D  Ktw alpha beta    gamma   delta  delta_obl epsilon epsilon_obl
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  CFRP Multiple Wall
  -   4.2   8.4   0.0   1.1   0.1   0.4   1.5   0.5   0.3333   0.6667   1.3333   1.33   0.0000   0.0
   2  SRL Example 2
  -   3.0   7.0   3.0   1.2   0.1   0.3   0.7   0.5   0.6667   0.3333   1.0000   1.20   2.9000   3.0
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
